  title: Ashoka
  text: Ashoka ruled from about 268 to 232 BCE. After the Kalinga war he turned to Buddhism and a policy of Dhamma. His edicts, carved on rocks and pillars across the subcontinent, are the earliest deciphered Indian inscriptions, mostly in Prakrit in the Brahmi script.
